  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend followed by a single positive sentiment spike; true outcomes often reverse sharply downward within the first 5 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "When sentiment history contains alternating high/low values (e.g., 1.00, -1.00) amidst volatile price action, the model's smooth upward drift consistently underestimates immediate volatility and fails to capture subsequent mean reversion toward historical averages.",
    "The model systematically over-projects linear growth in scenarios where recent sentiment is mixed or negative; true outcomes frequently show a 'spike-and-fall' pattern where prices rise briefly then drop below the forecasted path within 10 days.",
    "In volatile regimes (high standard deviation in last 18 days), the model's low-volatility linear extrapolation creates a persistent positive bias, requiring a downward correction of approximately 5-10% on the first day of the forecast horizon."
  ]
